IMPORT prelude

-- Texas Constitution, Article VIII -- the personal taxes the State may not impose: the individual income tax (s 24-a),
-- capital gains (s 24-b), wealth (s 25), and death and gift taxes (s 26). This is the Texas half of "personal income
-- tax": Texas has none, and the Constitution says so.
--
-- SEAT: the individual (an employee, a partner, an investor, an heir). "Can Texas tax my wages? My share of my partnership?
-- My capital gains? My net worth? My inheritance?" The prohibitions address the legislature; they are encoded for what they
-- mean for the individual, with one prohibition rule each so that the legislature's position is a parameter.
--
-- Edition: Tex. Const. art. VIII as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/tex-const-art8.txt (Texas Legislative
-- Council file dated 2026-07-31, amendments credited to 2025; retrieved 2026-10-19).
--
-- Federal income tax, and Texas's other taxes (sales, property, franchise), are outside this encoding. The federal
-- Internal Revenue Code encoding is at subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986/ (not imported).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Texas Constitution art. VIII -- personal taxes the legislature may not impose`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the legislature`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `impose a tax on the net incomes of individuals`
    `impose a tax on an individual's capital gains`
    `impose a tax based on wealth or net worth`
    `impose a death tax, or a new or increased tax on an estate, inheritance or gift transfer`

§§ `s 24-a -- the individual income tax`

-- s 24-a: "The legislature may not impose a tax on the net incomes of individuals, including an individual's share of
-- partnership and unincorporated association income." (Added Nov. 5, 2019.) No time limit: the prohibition stands until
-- the Constitution is amended.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`s 24-a -- no individual income tax` MEANS
    PARTY `the legislature`
    SHANT `impose a tax on the net incomes of individuals`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the legislature` BECAUSE "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a: the legislature may not impose a tax on the net incomes of individuals"

DECLARE `My income` IS ONE OF
    `wages or salary`
    `self-employment or business income as a sole proprietor`
    `my share of partnership or unincorporated association income`
    `interest, dividends or rent`
    `retirement income or Social Security`

DECLARE `Income answer` IS ONE OF
    `no: Texas may not tax the net incomes of individuals (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`
    `no: Texas may not tax an individual's share of partnership or unincorporated association income (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`

@export Can the State of Texas tax my income (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)?
GIVEN `the kind of income` IS A `My income` @desc The kind of income you are asking about: "wages or salary", "self-employment or business income as a sole proprietor", "my share of partnership or unincorporated association income", "interest, dividends or rent", or "retirement income or Social Security"
GIVETH AN `Income answer`
`Can Texas tax my income` MEANS
    IF `the kind of income` EQUALS `my share of partnership or unincorporated association income`
    THEN `no: Texas may not tax an individual's share of partnership or unincorporated association income (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`
    ELSE `no: Texas may not tax the net incomes of individuals (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-a)`

@export Must I file a Texas state income tax return or have Texas income tax withheld from my pay?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I file a Texas income tax return` MEANS FALSE

§§ `s 24-b -- capital gains`

-- s 24-b(a): "the legislature may not impose a tax on the realized or unrealized capital gains of an individual, family,
-- estate, or trust, including a tax on the sale or transfer of a capital asset that is payable by the individual, family,
-- estate, or trust selling or transferring the asset." (b): this does not modify or prohibit "(1) an ad valorem tax on
-- property; (2) a sales tax on the sale of goods or services; or (3) a use tax". (Added Nov. 4, 2025.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`s 24-b -- no capital gains tax` MEANS
    PARTY `the legislature`
    SHANT `impose a tax on an individual's capital gains`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the legislature` BECAUSE "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-b: the legislature may not impose a tax on the realized or unrealized capital gains of an individual, family, estate or trust"

DECLARE `Tax on a sale` IS ONE OF
    `a tax on my gain, realized or unrealized`
    `a tax on selling or transferring a capital asset, payable by me as seller`
    `property tax (ad valorem)`
    `sales tax or use tax on goods or services`

@export Can Texas tax my capital gains, or tax me for selling an asset (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 24-b)?
GIVEN `the kind of tax` IS A `Tax on a sale` @desc The tax you are asking about: "a tax on my gain, realized or unrealized", "a tax on selling or transferring a capital asset, payable by me as seller", "property tax (ad valorem)", or "sales tax or use tax on goods or services"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May Texas impose this tax on my sale or gain` IF
        `the kind of tax` EQUALS `property tax (ad valorem)`
    OR  `the kind of tax` EQUALS `sales tax or use tax on goods or services`

§§ `s 25 -- wealth`

-- s 25: "The legislature may not impose a tax based on the wealth or net worth of an individual or family, including a tax
-- based on the difference between the assets and liabilities of an individual or family." (Added Nov. 7, 2023.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`s 25 -- no wealth tax` MEANS
    PARTY `the legislature`
    SHANT `impose a tax based on wealth or net worth`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the legislature` BECAUSE "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 25: the legislature may not impose a tax based on the wealth or net worth of an individual or family"

@export Can Texas tax my wealth or net worth (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 25)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Can Texas tax my net worth` MEANS FALSE

§§ `s 26 -- death and gift taxes (when someone dies or gives me something)`

-- s 26(a): the legislature may not "(1) impose a state tax on the property of a deceased individual's estate because of the
-- death of the individual, including an estate, inheritance, or death tax; (2) impose a state tax on the transfer of an
-- estate, inheritance, legacy, succession, or gift ... if the tax was not in effect on January 1, 2025; or (3) increase the
-- rate or expand the applicability of a state tax described by Subdivision (2) ... that was in effect on January 1, 2025".
-- (b): it does not prohibit "(1) a tax described by Section 29(b) of this article; (2) a tax applicable to the transfer of a
-- motor vehicle by gift; or (3) an ad valorem tax on property". (Added Nov. 4, 2025.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`s 26 -- no death tax and no new transfer tax` MEANS
    PARTY `the legislature`
    SHANT `impose a death tax, or a new or increased tax on an estate, inheritance or gift transfer`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the legislature` BECAUSE "Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a): no estate, inheritance or death tax, and no transfer tax on an estate, inheritance, legacy, succession or gift unless in effect on 1 January 2025, and then not increased"

DECLARE `Transfer tax` IS ONE OF
    `a tax on a dead person's estate because of the death`
    `a tax on my inheritance, legacy, succession or a gift to me`
    `a tax on a motor vehicle I am given`
    `property tax on what I inherit`

DECLARE `Transfer answer` IS ONE OF
    `no (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a)(1))`
    `no, unless that tax was in effect on 1 January 2025, and then not at a higher rate or wider reach (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a)(2), (3))`
    `yes: s 26 does not prohibit it (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(b))`

@export Can Texas tax an estate, my inheritance or a gift to me (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26)?
GIVEN `the kind of tax` IS A `Transfer tax` @desc The tax you are asking about: "a tax on a dead person's estate because of the death", "a tax on my inheritance, legacy, succession or a gift to me", "a tax on a motor vehicle I am given", or "property tax on what I inherit"
GIVETH A `Transfer answer`
`Can Texas tax an estate, inheritance or gift` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of tax`
    WHEN `a tax on a dead person's estate because of the death` THEN `no (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a)(1))`
    WHEN `a tax on my inheritance, legacy, succession or a gift to me` THEN `no, unless that tax was in effect on 1 January 2025, and then not at a higher rate or wider reach (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(a)(2), (3))`
    OTHERWISE `yes: s 26 does not prohibit it (Tex. Const. art. VIII, s 26(b))`
